Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, with the new tools given the provisions of the law, such as take down provisions.

1900
02:20:16,540 --> 02:20:22,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So they will follow up with the DBM in terms of the budgetary support.

1901
02:20:22,320 --> 02:20:24,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And so they need.

1902
02:20:24,520 --> 02:20:26,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So they need the Senate's help in that regard.

1903
02:20:35,640 --> 02:20:39,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And the current budget was reduced.

1904
02:20:39,580 --> 02:20:40,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I mean the proposed budget.

1905
02:20:41,060 --> 02:20:43,680
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: If that can be restored, it will be a great help.

1906
02:20:43,900 --> 02:20:45,540
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Lalong-lalo na may bagong agency.

1907
02:20:46,500 --> 02:20:49,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dapat hindi na-cut at the minimum.

1908
02:20:51,900 --> 02:20:54,340
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Hindi na-cut at the minimum.

1909
02:20:54,520 --> 02:20:55,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: As is.

1910
02:20:55,540 --> 02:20:56,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Better yet, dagdag.

1911
02:20:57,740 --> 02:20:58,720
Senator Risa Hontiveros: I agree po.

1912
02:20:58,860 --> 02:21:00,460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good sponsor, Mr. President.

1913
02:21:01,140 --> 02:21:03,200
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Mas maigi kung madagdagan pa.

1914
02:21:03,200 --> 02:21:09,460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Laan po itong representasyon makipagtulungan sa good sponsor para makamit natin yan.

1915
02:21:10,020 --> 02:21:18,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Lalo na dahil gaya ng sinabi nyo, may bagong ahensyang nilika itong harinawa malapit ng maging batas ng batang ligtas.

1916
02:21:19,160 --> 02:21:24,060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At inilalaan nito, pinalakas pa yung mga tools na dati nang ginagamit ng department.

1917
02:21:24,520 --> 02:21:28,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Laban lalo na sa online sexual abuse and exploitation of children.

1918
02:21:28,880 --> 02:21:32,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Laban sa CISAEM.

1919
02:21:33,260 --> 02:21:38,160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At ilaan ang mga tools na ito at matutukan ng bagong ahensya.

1920
02:21:38,660 --> 02:21:44,640
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pati yung bagong banta sa ating mga bata online na nihilistic violent extremism.

1921
02:21:45,120 --> 02:21:47,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So maraming salamat po.

1922
02:21:47,560 --> 02:21:51,260
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Good sponsor, Mr. President at sa department.

1923
02:21:51,260 --> 02:21:54,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, thank you to Senator Riza Ontiveros, Mr. President.

1924
02:21:54,520 --> 02:21:55,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: I agree fully.

1925
02:21:57,460 --> 02:22:04,560
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: It's interesting to note that there seems to be conflicting signals.

1926
02:22:04,920 --> 02:22:11,440
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: You pass the new measure and yet you cut, you slash the budget of the predecessor agency.

1927
02:22:12,120 --> 02:22:17,080
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So we have to address the disconnect.

1928
02:22:17,080 --> 02:22:24,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And hopefully during the introduction of amendments, we can address the increase.

1929
02:22:24,520 --> 02:22:27,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Or restoration of the budget.

1930
02:22:28,360 --> 02:22:30,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. President.

1931
02:22:30,360 --> 02:22:31,720
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Senator Riza.

1932
02:22:31,800 --> 02:22:32,180
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

1933
02:22:32,780 --> 02:22:33,480
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Majority Leader.

1934
02:22:36,260 --> 02:22:39,920
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, with that, we have no other members who wish to interpolate.

1935
02:22:40,000 --> 02:22:46,160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: We also got the message from the Minority Floor Leader that they will no longer interpolate the budget of the DOJ.

1936
02:22:46,380 --> 02:22:54,080
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Therefore, I move, Mr. President, that the budget of the Department of Justice, Office of the Secretary, Bureau of Corrections,

1937
02:22:54,520 --> 02:23:00,260
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Bureau of Immigrations, Land Registration Authority, National Bureau of Investigations,

1938
02:23:00,900 --> 02:23:04,960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Office of Alternative Dispute Resolution, Office of the Government Corporate Council,

1939
02:23:05,720 --> 02:23:10,160
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Office of the Solicitor General, Parole and Probation Administration,

1940
02:23:11,240 --> 02:23:15,640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Presidential Commission on Good Government, and Public Attorney's Office be deemed submitted.

1941
02:23:15,800 --> 02:23:16,700
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I so move, Mr. President.

1942
02:23:16,700 --> 02:23:17,440
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection?

1943
02:23:18,400 --> 02:23:23,880
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hearing none, the budget of the Department of Justice and the attached agencies,

1944
02:23:24,040 --> 02:23:24,500
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: and mentioned.

1945
02:23:24,740 --> 02:23:28,200
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: The agency's budget is hereby deemed submitted.

1946
02:23:29,100 --> 02:23:30,320
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Congratulations to them.

1947
02:23:30,340 --> 02:23:30,620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Thank you.

1948
02:23:30,960 --> 02:23:32,140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May I ask for a minute's suspension?

1949
02:23:32,360 --> 02:23:33,120
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Session suspended.

1950
02:28:54,520 --> 02:29:04,040
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Mr. President, today we will have the hard-working men and women of the Department of Agrarian Reform

1951
02:29:04,040 --> 02:29:09,020
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: headed by no other than the legendary Secretary Conrad Estrella.

1952
02:29:11,880 --> 02:29:13,740
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Legendary Secretary.

1953
02:29:14,460 --> 02:29:20,960
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: Our dear friend, dear friend of the Senate President Pro Temp, dear friend of mine and my father's, Mr. President,

1954
02:29:20,960 --> 02:29:24,500
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: I just want to put on record that they've been doing a great job.

1955
02:29:24,520 --> 02:29:31,580
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: On their mandate in the Department of Agrarian Reform, one of our hard-working departments,

1956
02:29:31,960 --> 02:29:41,140
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: and continuously, continuously performing their duties in land transfers to the people in need.

1957
02:29:41,600 --> 02:29:44,760
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: So, Mr. President, I move that we take up their budget.

1958
02:29:45,300 --> 02:29:47,820
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Any objection?

1959
02:29:48,260 --> 02:29:52,620
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Hearing none, the budget of the Department of Agrarian Reform is hereby considered.

1960
02:29:52,620 --> 02:29:53,820
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: May we recognize that...

1961
02:29:54,520 --> 02:29:59,640
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: ...equally hard-working chairperson of the subcommittee.

1962
02:30:00,000 --> 02:30:04,620
Senator Juan Miguel "Migz" F. Zubiri: No other than Senator Kiko Pangilinan, our resident agriculturist, Mr. President.

1963
02:30:05,020 --> 02:30:08,800
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: My favorite nephew-in-law is recognized, Senator Pangilinan.

1964
02:30:08,800 --> 02:30:12,840
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Thank you, Mr. President. Thank you, Majority Leader.

1965
02:30:13,380 --> 02:30:27,120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ginoong Pangulo, sinusuportahan po natin ang panukalang budget ng Department of Agrarian Reform para sa 2027 na nagkakahalagang P16,121,735,000.

1966
02:30:27,120 --> 02:30:36,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang kabuhang pondo ng DAR, Puhunan sa Siguridad sa Lupa, Kabuhayan at Katatagan ng ating mga magsasaka.

1967
02:30:37,760 --> 02:30:44,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dinagdagan natin ng P1,700,000,000 sa bersyong ipinasa ng Kamara.

1968
02:30:44,620 --> 02:30:54,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kabilang dito ang P600,000,000 para sa Value Chain Information for Sustainable Transformation in Agrarian Reform Communities o VISTA.

1969
02:30:54,680 --> 02:30:57,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kabilang din ang P500,000,000.

1970
02:30:57,120 --> 02:31:05,120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: P500,000,000 bilang compensation sa mga may-ari ng lupa na saklaw ng reformang agraryo.

1971
02:31:06,140 --> 02:31:15,120
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: VISTA is a six-year initiative from 2025 to 2030 designed to improve the livelihoods of agrarian reform beneficiaries, ARBs,

1972
02:31:16,180 --> 02:31:21,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: through sustainable agriculture, enterprise development, and rural infrastructure.

1973
02:31:21,200 --> 02:31:26,200
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: May pagkahawig sa ating sagipsaka pero nakatutok sa 70,000 small...

1974
02:31:27,120 --> 02:31:31,320
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ...holder households sa mahigit 80 agrarian reform communities.

1975
02:31:31,580 --> 02:31:40,240
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Sa harap ng banta ng matinding El Niño, kasama rin sa VISTA ang paghahanda sa ating mga komunidad bago matuyo ang lupa.

1976
02:31:40,840 --> 02:31:48,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Palalakasin nito ang supply ng tubig, rainwater collection, agroforestry, at iba pang pamamaraan ng climate adaptation.

1977
02:31:50,000 --> 02:31:56,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Kasabay ng mga ito, papabilisin din ng pamamahagi ng lupa at palalakasin ang serbisyong legal...

1978
02:31:56,520 --> 02:31:57,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ... para makapag-aaral sa lupa.

1979
02:31:57,120 --> 02:32:04,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ang mga makinabang ang dapat makinabang, hindi ang mga makapangyarihang interes, kundi ang ating mga magsasaka.

1980
02:32:04,880 --> 02:32:12,880
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Mr. President, it is also my honor to defend the agrarian reform department budget,

1981
02:32:13,400 --> 02:32:21,300
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: considering that the Secretary is my schoolmate from the legendary LaSalle Green Hills.

1982
02:32:22,700 --> 02:32:24,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Animal LaSalle.

1983
02:32:24,040 --> 02:32:27,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: At handa na po tayong...

1984
02:32:27,120 --> 02:32:32,820
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: ... tumugon sa mga tanong ng ating butihing mga senador. Maraming salamat po.

1985
02:32:35,560 --> 02:32:38,260
Senator Vicente C. Sotto III: Majority Leader, Sen. Amy Marcos is recognized.

1986
02:32:39,000 --> 02:32:42,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes, thank you very much, Mr. President, Majority Leader, our Chairman.

1987
02:32:44,040 --> 02:32:53,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I simply want an update. As a long-standing agrarian reform advocate, I simply would like an update on the progress.

1988
02:32:53,860 --> 02:32:56,860
Senator Imee R. Marcos: We have reported time and again that the number of beneficiaries...

1989
02:32:57,120 --> 02:33:04,800
Senator Imee R. Marcos: ... from the condonation effort in 2023 was at 620,255 ARBs.

1990
02:33:05,320 --> 02:33:07,960
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ilan na ba ngayon at ilan pa ba ang pending?

1991
02:33:08,740 --> 02:33:15,740
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Kasi ang alam ko, may balance pa rin tayo dun sa 57.76 billion na target natin.

1992
02:33:16,140 --> 02:33:20,040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Parang kulang-kulang pa ng 3 billion worth. Tama ba yun?

1993
02:33:20,040 --> 02:33:24,040
Senator Imee R. Marcos: At ano ang plano natin para matapos na yan?

1994
02:33:27,120 --> 02:33:35,180
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: According to the Secretary, ang nakitira na namang ay ang nasa BARM.

1995
02:33:35,560 --> 02:33:36,920
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil hinihintay pa nila.

1996
02:33:39,400 --> 02:33:42,420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Ahinintay lang nila yung eleksyon. At since tapos na...

1997
02:33:42,420 --> 02:33:43,020
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos na.

1998
02:33:45,240 --> 02:33:53,480
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung buong 3 billion, lahat BARM yun. Malaki-laki to ha. 283,387 hectares. Lahat yan BARM?

1999
02:33:53,480 --> 02:33:55,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: That is correct, according to the Secretary.

2000
02:33:55,900 --> 02:33:57,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That entire balance.

2001
02:33:57,120 --> 02:34:05,460
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So we are awaiting BARM. And we look forward to the completion of this program.

2002
02:34:05,960 --> 02:34:10,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So yun yung update, yung isa pang update sana, yung tungkol sa VISTA project.

2003
02:34:11,340 --> 02:34:18,340
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yung VISTA project, yung Senate, through the Chair, restored the 600 million reduction of the House.

2004
02:34:18,700 --> 02:34:23,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ayan. Eto na yung mga foreign assistant projects na binabas bawatan.

2005
02:34:23,900 --> 02:34:27,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Para lang maintindihan natin at bakit rin restore ng House.

2006
02:34:27,120 --> 02:34:34,320
Senator Imee R. Marcos: What is the purpose of the project? It's a distinction from other existing livelihood and support projects.

2007
02:34:34,980 --> 02:34:37,840
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Ano yung kanyang pakay?

2008
02:34:41,340 --> 02:34:52,800
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, the VISTA, Value Chain Innovation for Sustainable Transformation in Agrarian Reform, precisely addresses the challenges of the supply chain.

2009
02:34:52,920 --> 02:34:53,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Oo nga.

2010
02:34:53,400 --> 02:34:56,860
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Dahil pag buhag-hag yung supply chain,

2011
02:34:57,120 --> 02:35:01,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: hindi maibibenta ng tama, hindi maibibenta sa tamang presyo,

2012
02:35:01,840 --> 02:35:06,500
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: o hindi maibibenta, titatapo na lamang ang ating mga produkto.

2013
02:35:06,640 --> 02:35:12,040
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, they have target beneficiaries of 80,000 smallholder households,

2014
02:35:12,560 --> 02:35:15,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and 400,000 individual beneficiaries.

2015
02:35:16,280 --> 02:35:22,940
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 50% of their beneficiaries are women, 30% are IMPs, and 20% kabataan.

2016
02:35:22,940 --> 02:35:26,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: To reduce rural poverty and increase food security,

2017
02:35:26,140 --> 02:35:29,280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: while protecting and enhancing the natural ecosystems.

2018
02:35:30,460 --> 02:35:34,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And of course, the clear objective is to increase income and employment,

2019
02:35:35,560 --> 02:35:41,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: and climate resilience of target groups in fragile upland areas,

2020
02:35:41,500 --> 02:35:43,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: including women, youth, and IPs,

2021
02:35:43,880 --> 02:35:46,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: through the strengthening of inclusive value chains,

2022
02:35:47,400 --> 02:35:50,700
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: with conservation and sustainable use of natural resources.

2023
02:35:50,700 --> 02:35:55,620
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry, it sounds very much like very similar livelihood and support services.

2024
02:35:56,140 --> 02:35:56,900
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, is it different?

2025
02:35:57,900 --> 02:35:59,820
Senator Imee R. Marcos: I think that was our question.

2026
02:35:59,820 --> 02:36:04,400
Senator Imee R. Marcos: It is concentrated on two regions, namely CAR and Region 12,

2027
02:36:04,600 --> 02:36:11,380
Senator Imee R. Marcos: and it focuses on two principal high-value crops, like coffee and camo.

2028
02:36:11,600 --> 02:36:15,020
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, it is focused on two regions.

2029
02:36:15,220 --> 02:36:18,280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: This would be CAR and Region 12.

2030
02:36:18,860 --> 02:36:19,640
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, it's CAR?

2031
02:36:19,640 --> 02:36:20,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Sorry.

2032
02:36:20,900 --> 02:36:22,000
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Region CAR.

2033
02:36:22,080 --> 02:36:25,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: CAR, okay. Cordillera and Region 12.

2034
02:36:25,240 --> 02:36:25,980
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And Region 12.

2035
02:36:26,140 --> 02:36:27,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That sucks our genes.

2036
02:36:27,240 --> 02:36:27,600
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

2037
02:36:27,820 --> 02:36:32,900
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And focused likewise on two principal crops,

2038
02:36:33,300 --> 02:36:36,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: high-value crops, coffee and cacao.

2039
02:36:36,520 --> 02:36:41,520
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, this is the focus, apart from the other programs.

2040
02:36:42,180 --> 02:36:43,520
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did the House cancel it?

2041
02:36:44,920 --> 02:36:48,080
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did the House cancel the counterpart?

2042
02:36:56,140 --> 02:37:02,600
DAR Secretary Conrado M. Estrella III: Our budget utilization rate is 92%.

2043
02:37:02,600 --> 02:37:23,400
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Actually, the Secretary, who is a long-standing alumnus of the House, said it looks like the House members made a mistake in that they did not appreciate the figures in terms of absorption and utilization.

2044
02:37:23,400 --> 02:37:26,120
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Bakit akala nila hindi na-disburse?

2045
02:37:26,140 --> 02:37:30,100
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: They thought that the amounts were not being disbursed.

2046
02:37:30,280 --> 02:37:31,940
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did that confusion occur?

2047
02:37:34,220 --> 02:37:39,420
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Because the release was delayed as in many other releases.

2048
02:37:41,180 --> 02:37:43,740
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: July was released this year.

2049
02:37:49,220 --> 02:37:54,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, it was released in July, but the actual implementation was in October.

2050
02:37:54,360 --> 02:37:55,060
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Okay.

2051
02:37:55,060 --> 02:37:55,360
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: But their...

2052
02:37:56,140 --> 02:37:58,640
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The utilization rate is, in fact, 92%.

2053
02:37:58,640 --> 02:37:59,780
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: 92%.

2054
02:37:59,780 --> 02:38:00,440
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

2055
02:38:00,820 --> 02:38:01,160
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Okay.

2056
02:38:01,360 --> 02:38:06,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: So, I think the Senate was right in restoring the 600 million.

2057
02:38:06,440 --> 02:38:10,060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: More importantly, what is the current status of the split project?

2058
02:38:10,660 --> 02:38:12,100
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Maraming umaasa sa split.

2059
02:38:12,620 --> 02:38:17,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The project was originally scheduled two years ago.

2060
02:38:17,300 --> 02:38:20,560
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Dapat nag-close na yan, December 31, 2024, diba?

2061
02:38:21,100 --> 02:38:25,300
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Tapos in-extend to December 31 na naman, 2027.

2062
02:38:26,140 --> 02:38:26,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Next year.

2063
02:38:27,720 --> 02:38:31,060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Why did we require a three-year extension period?

2064
02:38:31,700 --> 02:38:35,980
Senator Imee R. Marcos: And is the DAR now on track to meet the 2027 deadline?

2065
02:38:36,340 --> 02:38:38,140
Senator Imee R. Marcos: That's already an extended deadline.

2066
02:38:39,480 --> 02:38:42,620
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes, we are full speed ahead, according to the Secretary.

2067
02:38:43,060 --> 02:38:46,140
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: The reason for the delay was the pandemic.

2068
02:38:46,880 --> 02:38:48,260
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: And because of...

2069
02:38:48,260 --> 02:38:53,580
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: So, the reason for the delay primarily was because of COVID, the pandemic.

2070
02:38:54,420 --> 02:38:55,060
Senator Imee R. Marcos: The COVID.

2071
02:38:55,060 --> 02:38:55,280
Senator Francis Kiko Pangilinan: Yes.

2072
02:38:55,280 --> 02:38:55,920
Senator Imee R. Marcos: Yes.

